---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalSubnav from '../components/LegalSubnav.astro';
import { getSite } from '../lib/site';

const { legalEmail } = getSite();

const description =
  'Terms & Conditions for the Bycon Transport Management System, related sites and apps, including SMS and acceptable use.';
---
<Layout title="Terms & Conditions" description={description}>
  <article class="prose terms-doc">
    <LegalSubnav current="terms" />

    <header class="terms-header">
      <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="effective-date"><strong>Effective date:</strong> March 29, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <p>
      These Terms &amp; Conditions (“Terms”) govern your access to and use of the Transport Management System and related
      websites, applications, and services (collectively, the “Services”) offered by or on behalf of{' '}
      <strong>Bycon</strong> (“Operator,” “we,” “us,” or “our”). By accessing or using the Services, you agree to these Terms.
      If you do not agree, do not use the Services.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you use the Services on behalf of an organization, you represent that you have authority to bind that organization,
      and “you” includes that organization.
    </p>

    <section class="terms-section" id="services" aria-labelledby="h-services">
      <h2 id="h-services">1. The Services</h2>
      <p>
        The Services support transportation and workforce operations, which may include scheduling, dispatch-related features,
        driver or staff tools, timesheets, document handling, and communications such as email or SMS notifications. Features
        vary by deployment and user role. We may modify, suspend, or discontinue any part of the Services with reasonable
        notice where practicable.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section" id="eligibility" aria-labelledby="h-eligibility">
      <h2 id="h-eligibility">2. Eligibility and accounts</h2>
      <p>
        You must provide accurate registration information and keep credentials confidential. You are responsible for activity
        under your account. Notify us promptly at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${legalEmail}`}>{legalEmail}</a> if you suspect unauthorized access.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section" id="sms-terms" aria-labelledby="h-sms-terms">
      <h2 id="h-sms-terms">3. Text messaging (SMS) terms</h2>
      <p>
        By providing your mobile number and opting in where consent is required, you consent to receive text messages from us
        relating to the Services as described at the point of collection (for example, trip updates or operational notices).
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Frequency:</strong> Message frequency varies based on your interactions and service settings.</li>
        <li><strong>Cost:</strong> Message and data rates may apply; contact your carrier with questions about your plan.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Opt-out:</strong> You may opt out of promotional texts as instructed in those messages (e.g., STOP).
          Operational messages may continue where permitted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Support:</strong> Reply HELP or email{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${legalEmail}`}>{legalEmail}</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Carriers:</strong> Participating carriers may change; we are not responsible for delays or failures by carriers
          or networks.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Our collection and use of phone numbers and related data is described in our{' '}
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section" id="acceptable-use" aria-labelledby="h-acceptable-use">
      <h2 id="h-acceptable-use">4. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Violate law or third-party rights;</li>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Services, other accounts, or our systems;</li>
        <li>Interfere with or disrupt the Services or infrastructure;</li>
        <li>Use the Services to send spam, unlawful, or misleading communications;</li>
        <li>Reverse engineer, scrape, or misuse the Services except as permitted by applicable law;</li>
        <li>Use the Services in any way that could harm passengers, the public, or transportation safety.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section" id="content" aria-labelledby="h-content">
      <h2 id="h-content">5. Content and data</h2>
      <p>
        You retain your rights in content you submit. You grant us a license to use, store, and process such content as needed
        to provide and improve the Services and comply with law. You represent that you have the rights necessary to grant
        this license.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section" id="third-party" aria-labelledby="h-third-party">
      <h2 id="h-third-party">6. Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        The Services may integrate with or link to third-party services (maps, messaging providers, payment processors, etc.).
        Those services are governed by their own terms and privacy policies; we are not responsible for third-party services.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section" id="disclaimers" aria-labelledby="h-disclaimers">
      <h2 id="h-disclaimers">7. Disclaimers</h2>
      <p class="terms-legalcaps">
        THE SERVICES ARE PROVIDED “AS IS” AND “AS AVAILABLE” WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, WHETHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
        INCLUDING IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT, TO THE FULLEST
        EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW. TRANSPORTATION SERVICES MAY BE PROVIDED BY THIRD PARTIES; THE OPERATOR’S SOFTWARE DOES NOT
        REPLACE COMPLIANCE WITH APPLICABLE TRANSPORTATION, SAFETY, OR INSURANCE REQUIREMENTS.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section" id="liability" aria-labelledby="h-liability">
      <h2 id="h-liability">8. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p class="terms-legalcaps">
        TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE OPERATOR AND ITS AFFILIATES, OFFICERS, EMPLOYEES, AND SUPPLIERS WILL NOT BE
        LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, OR
        GOODWILL, ARISING FROM OR RELATED TO YOUR USE OF THE SERVICES. OUR AGGREGATE LIABILITY FOR CLAIMS ARISING OUT OF OR
        RELATING TO THE SERVICES OR THESE TERMS WILL NOT EXCEED THE GREATER OF (A) THE AMOUNTS YOU PAID US FOR THE SERVICES IN
        THE TWELVE (12) MONTHS BEFORE THE CLAIM OR (B) ONE HUNDRED U.S. DOLLARS (US$100), IF NO FEES WERE PAID. SOME
        JURISDICTIONS DO NOT ALLOW CERTAIN LIMITATIONS; IN THOSE CASES, OUR LIABILITY WILL BE LIMITED TO THE FULLEST EXTENT
        PERMITTED BY LAW.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section" id="indemnity" aria-labelledby="h-indemnity">
      <h2 id="h-indemnity">9. Indemnity</h2>
      <p>
        You will defend, indemnify, and hold harmless the Operator and its affiliates from claims, damages, losses, and
        expenses (including reasonable attorneys’ fees) arising from your use of the Services, your content, or your violation
        of these Terms, except to the extent caused by our gross negligence or willful misconduct.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section" id="termination" aria-labelledby="h-termination">
      <h2 id="h-termination">10. Termination</h2>
      <p>
        We may suspend or terminate access to the Services for violation of these Terms or for operational or legal reasons. You
        may stop using the Services at any time. Provisions that by their nature should survive (including disclaimers,
        limitations, indemnity, and governing law) will survive termination.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section" id="law" aria-labelledby="h-law">
      <h2 id="h-law">11. Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the United States and the state in which the Operator is organized, without
        regard to conflict-of-law rules, except where mandatory consumer protection laws of your jurisdiction apply. Courts in
        that state (or federal courts located there, if applicable) will have exclusive jurisdiction for disputes, unless a
        different forum is required by law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section" id="changes" aria-labelledby="h-changes">
      <h2 id="h-changes">12. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. We will post the revised Terms with an updated effective date. Continued
        use after changes become effective constitutes acceptance, except where applicable law requires additional consent.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-section" id="contact" aria-labelledby="h-contact">
      <h2 id="h-contact">13. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms: <strong>Bycon</strong>,{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${legalEmail}`}>{legalEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="terms-footnote">
      These Terms are a practical template for a transportation-related software service. They are not a substitute for legal
      advice; have them reviewed by qualified counsel for your organization and jurisdiction.
    </p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .terms-doc {
      max-width: 42rem;
    }
    .terms-header {
      margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    }
    .terms-header h1 {
      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    }
    .effective-date {
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    }
    .terms-section h2 {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin: 1.75rem 0 0.5rem;
      scroll-margin-top: 4rem;
    }
    .terms-legalcaps {
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
      letter-spacing: 0.01em;
      padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
      background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.03);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .terms-footnote {
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-top: 2rem;
      padding-top: 1.25rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
